==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|NL.}} *palliativus, from {{etyl|ML.}} {{term|palliare||to cloak}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|pallium|lang=la||a cloak}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpalɪətɪv/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{medicine}} Minimising the progression of a [[disease]] and relieving [[undesirable]] [[symptoms]] for as long as possible, rather than attempting to cure the (usually [[incurable]]) disease.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|medicine}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|medicine}} [[analgesic]], [[lenitive]]

====Related terms====
* [[palliate]]
* [[palliation]]

====Translations====
{{trans-top|reducing progression and relieving symptoms}}
* Czech: {{t+|cs|paliativní}}
* Greek: {{t+|el|καταπραϋντικό|n|tr=katapra'intikó}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Hebrew: {{t-|he|מקל|m|tr=makel}}
* Portuguese: {{t+|pt|paliativo|m}}, {{t|pt|paliativa|f}}
* Swedish: {{t|sv|lindrande}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===See also===
* {{pedia|Palliative care}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{medicine}} Something that [[palliate]]s, particularly a palliative [[medicine]].
#: ''The radiation and chemotherapy were only '''palliatives'''.''

